1
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:34,570
<i>Timing and subtitles by the</i> 👠 Se Mi Secrets 🕶️ <i>Team @viki.com</i>

2
00:00:41,967 --> 00:00:45,033
[This drama is fictional, and any resemblance
to real people or events is coincidental.]

3
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:46,767
[Episode 8]
Come on!

4
00:00:46,767 --> 00:00:48,267
Dad.

5
00:00:48,267 --> 00:00:50,300
Excuse me, teachers.

6
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:55,067
We have a new driver
for our shuttle bus from now on.

7
00:00:55,067 --> 00:00:57,600
Mr. Gil, come over here for a second.

8
00:01:00,567 --> 00:01:02,400
Please take a moment to greet them.

9
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:04,133
Oh, my.

10
00:01:07,933 --> 00:01:08,933
Pleased to meet you.

11
00:01:08,933 --> 00:01:11,833
My name is Gil Ho Se.

12
00:01:11,833 --> 00:01:13,833
- Hello.
- Hello.

13
00:01:13,833 --> 00:01:17,200
Let's all work well together this month.

14
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:19,533
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

15
00:01:19,533 --> 00:01:21,367
Was it difficult to memorize
the children's addresses?

16
00:01:21,367 --> 00:01:24,200
No, that's part of my job.

17
00:01:25,967 --> 00:01:28,000
Please take good care of
the afternoon drop-offs too.

18
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,833
Yes, Principal.

19
00:01:31,067 --> 00:01:32,467
- Let's go in.
- Let's go.

20
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:36,767
A thief has appeared! Catch the thief!

21
00:01:38,567 --> 00:01:40,067
Principal.

22
00:01:40,067 --> 00:01:41,500
Yes.

23
00:01:42,967 --> 00:01:45,767
How did you find Mr. Gil Ho Se?

24
00:01:45,767 --> 00:01:47,367
From a job recruitment site.

25
00:01:47,367 --> 00:01:50,933
Before his leg injury, he worked
at several transport companies.

26
00:01:50,933 --> 00:01:53,300
Could I see his resume?

27
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:54,333
Why?

28
00:01:54,333 --> 00:01:56,400
Does something seem off?

29
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:00,133
He's a stranger.

30
00:02:00,133 --> 00:02:01,867
I'm concerned about my identity being exposed.

31
00:02:01,867 --> 00:02:03,733
Oh, my.

32
00:02:03,733 --> 00:02:05,433
I hadn't considered that.

33
00:02:05,433 --> 00:02:08,133
Let's go. It's in the principal's office.

34
00:02:14,367 --> 00:02:16,833
Here it is.

35
00:02:16,833 --> 00:02:21,000
I'll go teach the class,
so take your time checking.

36
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,667
- Okay.
- Okay.

37
00:02:29,012 --> 00:02:30,920
[Daehwang Transport]

38
00:02:31,367 --> 00:02:33,700
Daehwang Transport.

39
00:02:37,267 --> 00:02:39,400
<i>Hello, this is the Daehwang Transport office.</i>

40
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:44,133
I'd like to check the background
of someone who worked there before.

41
00:02:44,133 --> 00:02:45,667
His name is Gil Ho Se.

42
00:02:45,667 --> 00:02:48,867
<i>We keep records for only five years.</i>

43
00:02:48,867 --> 00:02:51,567
<i>If he worked here before that,
it would be difficult to verify.</i>

44
00:02:51,567 --> 00:02:54,067
[Daehwang Transport 2015.10-2018.11]
<i>What was his employment period?</i>

45
00:02:54,067 --> 00:02:56,700
[Work History]
Ah, seven years ago.

46
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:59,300
Okay, I understand, thank you.

47
00:03:08,033 --> 00:03:12,267
Sorry, I thought the principal was here.

48
00:03:12,267 --> 00:03:14,000
How can I help you?

49
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,833
Oh, the vehicle needs its scheduled maintenance.

50
00:03:17,833 --> 00:03:21,533
So, I need to get it done
before the afternoon drop-offs.

51
00:03:21,533 --> 00:03:23,200
I'll let the principal know.

52
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:26,800
Oh, thank you.

53
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:29,400
- Thank you for your hard work.
- Oh, okay.

54
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:46,400
[Geumcheon Labor]
Hurry up!

55
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:49,000
Captain.

56
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,933
That person over there.
I've never seen him before.

57
00:03:51,933 --> 00:03:53,200
Is he a total newbie?

58
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:54,667
Oh, him?

59
00:03:54,667 --> 00:03:57,300
It's his first time here,
but he's worked many other places.

60
00:03:57,300 --> 00:03:59,233
Try giving him a task, see how he does.

61
00:04:02,067 --> 00:04:05,233
If he can't handle it, he'll be out right away, you know?

62
00:04:05,233 --> 00:04:08,300
By the way, what's going on
with the Silver Town construction?

63
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:10,033
We need to get it done so we can make a living.

64
00:04:10,033 --> 00:04:11,767
Ugh, just wait a bit.

65
00:04:11,767 --> 00:04:14,667
That's giving me headaches too.

66
00:04:14,667 --> 00:04:17,467
But I'm going to wrap it up before this winter.

67
00:04:17,467 --> 00:04:19,833
- I'm counting on you.
- Yes.

68
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:26,700
So exciting.

69
00:04:27,367 --> 00:04:29,433
Ms. Bu, are you going with us today?

70
00:04:29,433 --> 00:04:32,600
- Yeah, I'm the one dropping them off today.
- Oh, okay.

71
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:34,167
I'll close the door.

72
00:04:34,167 --> 00:04:35,600
I love it most.

73
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:37,167
- Me too.
- Absolutely love it.

74
00:04:37,167 --> 00:04:40,367
Oh? Ms. Bu Se Mi's sitting in front of me.

75
00:04:40,367 --> 00:04:42,133
Ms. Bu Se Mi's sitting next to me.

76
00:04:42,133 --> 00:04:45,233
- I'm riding with Ms. Bu.
- But aren't you sitting in the back?

77
00:04:45,233 --> 00:04:47,000
Today is great.

78
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,633
Alright, everyone.

79
00:04:48,633 --> 00:04:50,933
Shall we sing our kindergarten song together?

80
00:04:50,933 --> 00:04:52,433
- Yes.
- Yes.

81
00:04:52,433 --> 00:04:55,900
- Start.
- S, s, start.

82
00:04:55,900 --> 00:05:02,100
<i>♪ Embracing the green energy of the mountains,
our Muchang Iseon Kindergarten ♪</i>

83
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:06,633
[Muchang Supermarket]

84
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:14,633
- Bye.
- See you tomorrow.

85
00:05:14,633 --> 00:05:17,967
- Bye-bye.
- See you.

86
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:20,033
Hae Na's mom.

87
00:05:20,033 --> 00:05:22,800
Mom, I'm home.

88
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:32,933
Huh? Oh. You came today, huh?

89
00:05:32,933 --> 00:05:35,633
Ms. Jenny has a lot of work to do.

90
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:40,733
I haven't seen those people before, right?

91
00:05:41,267 --> 00:05:44,100
It's the busy season, so Seong Tae brought them.

92
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:46,533
There's a shortage of workers in the countryside.

93
00:05:46,533 --> 00:05:48,033
It must be a lot of work.

94
00:05:48,033 --> 00:05:50,000
I'll go now.

95
00:05:51,333 --> 00:05:52,900
Goodbye.

96
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:55,300
Thank you. Miss, goodbye.

97
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:58,200
- Take care.
- Okay.

98
00:06:05,733 --> 00:06:08,500
Ju Won's house is the last one.

99
00:06:09,133 --> 00:06:12,233
Mr. Gil, I'll get off with Ju Won this time.

100
00:06:12,233 --> 00:06:13,367
Oh, you too?

101
00:06:13,367 --> 00:06:16,233
- Yes.
- She lives with us.

102
00:06:16,233 --> 00:06:18,000
Ah, really?

103
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,967
Wow, Ju Won. It must be nice.

104
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:29,100
We've arrived.

105
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:34,000
Alright, we've arrived.

106
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:37,067
Ju Won, let's go home.

107
00:06:38,167 --> 00:06:39,167
Let's go.

108
00:06:39,167 --> 00:06:41,467
- Thank you.
- Yes, Miss. Goodbye.

109
00:06:41,467 --> 00:06:42,900
See you tomorrow, Ju Won.

110
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:44,633
Yes.

111
00:06:46,967 --> 00:06:48,467
- Bye.
- See you.

112
00:06:48,467 --> 00:06:50,000
Yes.

113
00:07:01,367 --> 00:07:02,500
Ju Won, let's go.

114
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:04,267
Yes.

115
00:07:04,267 --> 00:07:05,567
[Psychopath]

116
00:07:05,567 --> 00:07:07,700
She didn't even check the message.

117
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:15,067
That woman's all talk, isn't she?

118
00:07:33,167 --> 00:07:36,233
That money from my daughter is all my money.

119
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:54,333
Yeong Ran.

120
00:07:54,333 --> 00:07:58,667
You're going to inherit that old man,
Chairman Ga Sung Ho's wealth, right?

121
00:07:58,667 --> 00:08:00,567
I've thought about it.

122
00:08:00,567 --> 00:08:04,933
And how about 10 million won a month,
on the condition that I stay quiet?

123
00:08:04,933 --> 00:08:08,667
I looked it up online,
and that old man has a ton of assets.

124
00:08:08,667 --> 00:08:11,500
If we're talking about 10 million won a month

125
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:15,433
for the maintenance of Chairman Ga Sung Ho's
mother-in-law's dignity, that's a real bargain.

126
00:08:15,433 --> 00:08:17,033
Don't you agree?

127
00:08:19,367 --> 00:08:22,000
I'll give you a week.

128
00:08:23,067 --> 00:08:25,400
Think carefully.

129
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:29,367
Yeong Ran.

130
00:08:39,900 --> 00:08:43,200
Lee Don seems to be playing games.

131
00:08:48,267 --> 00:08:51,900
[Seon Woo]

132
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:02,400
How long has he been holed up in the hotel?

133
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:04,333
<i>Sis, it's me.</i>

134
00:09:05,933 --> 00:09:08,067
Seon Woo.

135
00:09:08,067 --> 00:09:09,300
Where are you right now?

136
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:12,167
<i>Shut up now and listen carefully.</i>

137
00:09:12,167 --> 00:09:15,300
About those shares you have,

138
00:09:15,300 --> 00:09:17,800
transfer all of them to me.

139
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:20,600
What does that even mean?

140
00:09:21,133 --> 00:09:22,767
<i>'What does that even mean?'</i>

141
00:09:22,767 --> 00:09:27,233
Don't pretend you don't know, again!

142
00:09:29,100 --> 00:09:31,400
Don't you remember that day?

143
00:09:32,533 --> 00:09:35,233
The day Ye Rim died.

144
00:09:35,233 --> 00:09:37,833
<i>You were in New York, right?</i>

145
00:09:40,467 --> 00:09:41,867
Well.

146
00:09:41,867 --> 00:09:45,233
I happen to have a video from that day.

147
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:50,067
Seon Woo.

148
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:52,933
Let's meet and talk.

149
00:09:52,933 --> 00:09:53,833
<i>How about it?</i>

150
00:09:53,833 --> 00:09:58,533
If you accept my offer, come to Suite 858,
Sujeong Hotel, right now.

151
00:09:58,533 --> 00:10:00,933
If you refuse my offer,

152
00:10:01,467 --> 00:10:03,767
I'll just send this to Kim Yeong Ran.

153
00:10:03,767 --> 00:10:05,600
<i>Do as you will.</i>

154
00:10:11,933 --> 00:10:16,133
[Seon Woo]

155
00:10:25,267 --> 00:10:29,033
Wow... These siblings, really...

156
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:35,467
Seon Woo is in Suite 858 at Sujeong Hotel.

157
00:10:35,467 --> 00:10:38,500
No matter what it takes,
bring him to me right now.

158
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:40,467
Yes, Professor.

159
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:47,500
[Ms. Bu Se Mi]

160
00:10:50,033 --> 00:10:53,033
[Gil Ho Se's Resume]

161
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:00,533
-Yes?
-<i>Madam.</i>

162
00:11:00,533 --> 00:11:03,700
<i>Ga Seon Woo has decisive evidence</i>

163
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:05,167
<i>that Ga Seon Yeong is involved in Ye Rim's death.</i>

164
00:11:05,167 --> 00:11:06,833
Is that evidence reliable?

165
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:09,433
Yes, I've verified it.

166
00:11:09,433 --> 00:11:11,167
If we secure this evidence,

167
00:11:11,167 --> 00:11:14,600
this game will end quickly without any bloodshed.

168
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:15,967
Yes, understood.

169
00:11:15,967 --> 00:11:18,367
For now, please secure the evidence, Attorney Lee.

170
00:11:18,367 --> 00:11:22,233
But I'll follow through
on the promise I made to Chairman.

171
00:11:22,233 --> 00:11:23,633
<i>Understood, Madam.</i>

172
00:11:23,633 --> 00:11:26,667
Things are turning in our favor,

173
00:11:26,667 --> 00:11:29,700
so please stay alive.

174
00:12:04,567 --> 00:12:06,533
What's with the bouquet?

175
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:11,300
- Is it for confession?
- Be quiet.

176
00:12:11,300 --> 00:12:13,000
Oh, jeez.

177
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:17,233
Where is she rushing off to?

178
00:12:17,233 --> 00:12:20,100
Hey, I've got an emergency. I'll be back.

179
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:21,900
Good luck with your confession.

180
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:23,933
Dong Min, hey.

181
00:12:34,060 --> 00:12:36,267
Where did she go?

182
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:43,100
Corn.

183
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:45,600
When the corn grows tall, tall, tall,

184
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:47,733
pick the corn, knock, knock, knock,

185
00:12:47,733 --> 00:12:49,867
peel off the husk, shuck, shuck, shuck,

186
00:12:49,867 --> 00:12:51,933
then the corn is plump, plump, plump!

187
00:12:51,933 --> 00:12:53,333
You startled me.

188
00:12:53,333 --> 00:12:55,133
Ms. Baek Hye Ji.

189
00:12:55,133 --> 00:12:57,100
Make some noise when you walk!

190
00:12:57,100 --> 00:12:58,633
I'm the owner of this house,

191
00:12:58,633 --> 00:13:02,433
yet I feel like a squatter in my own home.

192
00:13:02,433 --> 00:13:04,767
Oh, what a scare.

193
00:13:04,767 --> 00:13:10,100
Nobody here is normal, including Madam.

194
00:13:10,100 --> 00:13:11,333
Ugh, what should I do?

195
00:13:11,333 --> 00:13:15,267
[Practical Assignment for 'Field Practice']
I need to upload this quickly.

196
00:13:21,333 --> 00:13:23,900
The moon today

197
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:27,267
is dark tonight.

198
00:14:42,367 --> 00:14:43,667
Who are you?

199
00:14:43,667 --> 00:14:45,800
Answer me!

200
00:14:53,900 --> 00:14:55,533
Miss.

201
00:15:03,430 --> 00:15:05,133
- Are you okay?
- There.

202
00:15:05,133 --> 00:15:06,767
There...

203
00:15:25,300 --> 00:15:27,033
He disappeared near here, right?

204
00:15:27,033 --> 00:15:28,633
Yes.

205
00:15:29,733 --> 00:15:31,100
By the way, where are we?

206
00:15:31,100 --> 00:15:32,600
It's the lodging for the farmhands.

207
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:34,433
I think the only place he could run to is here.

208
00:15:34,433 --> 00:15:36,867
-I'll go check it out.
-Oh, wait a minute.

209
00:15:36,867 --> 00:15:39,000
This is the men's lodging. I'll go check.

210
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:41,133
Wait here for a bit.

211
00:15:44,633 --> 00:15:47,267
No, that's not it.

212
00:15:47,267 --> 00:15:49,267
It's not.

213
00:16:12,567 --> 00:16:14,567
Who are you looking for?

214
00:16:14,567 --> 00:16:17,500
Oh, nothing.

215
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:33,600
There is someone suspicious, though.

216
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:37,133
It's late today, so I'll check with Seong Tae tomorrow.

217
00:16:37,133 --> 00:16:39,100
Let's call it a day for now.

218
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:40,967
That person had a scar on their collarbone.

219
00:16:40,967 --> 00:16:42,833
It would be useful if you remembered that too.

220
00:16:42,833 --> 00:16:45,200
A scar on the collarbone...

221
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:47,033
Got it.

222
00:16:47,567 --> 00:16:49,533
Wait.

223
00:16:49,533 --> 00:16:51,933
Give me your phone.

224
00:16:51,933 --> 00:16:53,567
My phone?

225
00:16:53,567 --> 00:16:55,533
Why do you need my phone?

226
00:16:55,533 --> 00:16:58,667
How am I saved in your contacts?

227
00:16:59,400 --> 00:17:01,267
Jeon Dong Min.

228
00:17:01,267 --> 00:17:03,300
Jeon Dong Min?

229
00:17:04,267 --> 00:17:07,500
Not Mr. Jeon Dong Min, not Mr. Jeon, not Teacher.

230
00:17:07,500 --> 00:17:10,567
You really typed it honestly, huh?

231
00:17:10,567 --> 00:17:14,033
I set up a speed dial for you.

232
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:16,433
If there's an emergency, just press 1.

233
00:17:16,433 --> 00:17:19,333
I'll get there faster than the police, okay?

234
00:17:19,933 --> 00:17:22,433
No need for this stuff.

235
00:17:27,733 --> 00:17:30,900
Wow, her personality is something else.

236
00:17:49,830 --> 00:17:52,133
Tae Min, what are you doing there?

237
00:17:58,700 --> 00:18:02,300
Oh, this, this thing.

238
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,867
The one you mentioned last time.

239
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:13,100
-Tae Min.
-Yes.

240
00:18:14,233 --> 00:18:16,567
You like me, right?

241
00:18:16,567 --> 00:18:18,333
Well.

242
00:18:20,900 --> 00:18:23,067
Oh, that's...

243
00:18:24,067 --> 00:18:26,367
Oh, wait. No.

244
00:18:26,367 --> 00:18:30,733
No, not now. No.

245
00:18:36,830 --> 00:18:42,467
Baek Hye Ji.

246
00:18:42,467 --> 00:18:44,167
Yes.

247
00:18:48,867 --> 00:18:53,900
I admire her.

248
00:18:58,733 --> 00:19:01,967
-General.
-Why?

249
00:19:03,230 --> 00:19:06,133
People don't confess like that these days.

250
00:19:06,667 --> 00:19:08,400
It's old-fashioned.

251
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:10,433
Old-fashioned?

252
00:19:11,033 --> 00:19:14,567
I don't care about what's trendy.

253
00:19:14,567 --> 00:19:18,500
Tae Min's been worried sick about you.

254
00:19:18,500 --> 00:19:21,167
Just remember that.

255
00:19:30,430 --> 00:19:31,833
This...

256
00:19:31,833 --> 00:19:34,267
Huh? General.

257
00:19:34,833 --> 00:19:36,767
- Tae Min.
- Yes.

258
00:19:36,767 --> 00:19:40,200
I'm tired. I'm going inside.

259
00:19:40,900 --> 00:19:44,533
Wait.

260
00:19:44,533 --> 00:19:46,567
General! General!

261
00:19:46,567 --> 00:19:49,367
Please, was that a confession or not?

262
00:19:49,367 --> 00:19:52,933
What do I do?

263
00:20:04,033 --> 00:20:05,767
Mom.

264
00:21:21,728 --> 00:21:23,733
[Answer, Door Open]

265
00:21:23,733 --> 00:21:27,033
Ugh, where are they?

266
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:34,900
Why aren't they here yet?

267
00:21:48,667 --> 00:21:52,533
I knew Ga Seon Yeong wouldn't come herself.

268
00:21:54,333 --> 00:21:56,667
I can't let Ga Seon Woo get caught.

269
00:22:01,833 --> 00:22:03,633
Vice President.

270
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:07,900
Open the door!

271
00:22:07,900 --> 00:22:09,867
Vice President.

272
00:22:12,633 --> 00:22:13,960
[Answer, Door Open]

273
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:15,400
Open up.

274
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:17,000
What?

275
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:19,967
Only Secretary Han came?

276
00:22:20,864 --> 00:22:22,495
Shoot!

277
00:22:23,500 --> 00:22:25,167
Yeah.

278
00:22:25,167 --> 00:22:28,367
My sister always does this.

279
00:22:28,367 --> 00:22:31,933
You think I don't know you're trying to
lock me up and kill me like Dad?

280
00:22:34,633 --> 00:22:36,333
Come out.

281
00:22:39,567 --> 00:22:41,500
Vice President.

282
00:22:43,933 --> 00:22:45,667
Come out.

283
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:53,733
Vice President.

284
00:22:53,733 --> 00:22:55,733
Come out.

285
00:22:55,733 --> 00:22:57,333
Huh?

286
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:04,733
Vice President.

287
00:23:11,433 --> 00:23:13,300
Vice President.

288
00:23:25,272 --> 00:23:29,432
Excuse me, let me get it for you.

289
00:23:34,367 --> 00:23:35,800
- Fire!
- Fire!

290
00:23:35,800 --> 00:23:36,867
Fire, fire!

291
00:23:36,867 --> 00:23:38,600
- Fire, fire!
- Get away from the fire.

292
00:23:38,600 --> 00:23:42,233
Get away from the fire.

293
00:23:43,333 --> 00:23:44,967
Go that way.

294
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:49,533
Fire!

295
00:23:57,376 --> 00:24:00,333
- Darn. Get out quickly!
- Oh, no.

296
00:24:00,333 --> 00:24:02,033
Let's go.

297
00:24:08,867 --> 00:24:10,833
You want to give it a shot?

298
00:24:12,300 --> 00:24:14,933
I'm not going to sit still anymore.

299
00:24:46,100 --> 00:24:47,833
What is that?

300
00:24:47,833 --> 00:24:49,500
It's a list of today's tasks.

301
00:24:49,500 --> 00:24:51,033
First, let's go to Seong Tae,

302
00:24:51,033 --> 00:24:55,267
get information about people
who came from outside.

303
00:24:55,267 --> 00:24:56,933
Okay.

304
00:24:56,933 --> 00:24:58,400
About that guy from yesterday.

305
00:24:58,400 --> 00:25:00,767
You mentioned he had a scar
on his collarbone, right?

306
00:25:00,767 --> 00:25:02,600
Which side was it on?

307
00:25:03,767 --> 00:25:05,167
<i>Who are you?</i>

308
00:25:05,167 --> 00:25:07,067
<i>Answer me!</i>

309
00:25:08,600 --> 00:25:10,833
- The left.
- Left.

310
00:25:10,833 --> 00:25:14,367
A scar on the left collarbone.

311
00:25:15,267 --> 00:25:18,067
Probably someone athletic.

312
00:25:18,067 --> 00:25:19,900
I'll keep a close eye out.

313
00:25:19,900 --> 00:25:21,500
Let's go.

314
00:25:25,333 --> 00:25:27,867
We need to do it as soon as possible.

315
00:25:27,867 --> 00:25:29,333
Okay?

316
00:25:29,333 --> 00:25:30,333
Seong Tae.

317
00:25:30,333 --> 00:25:31,933
It's just that I heard from someone

318
00:25:31,933 --> 00:25:35,567
that your people have a great reputation
for doing good work.

319
00:25:35,567 --> 00:25:36,733
They really are good.

320
00:25:36,733 --> 00:25:38,633
So, by the way,

321
00:25:38,633 --> 00:25:42,800
if you have any contact details or personal info,
could you share them with me?

322
00:25:44,433 --> 00:25:46,633
You're just asking for that?

323
00:25:46,633 --> 00:25:49,233
By the way, Hae Na left her pencil case yesterday.

324
00:25:49,233 --> 00:25:52,300
I was thinking of dropping it off
when I head to the supermarket.

325
00:25:52,300 --> 00:25:54,967
I'll text you right away.

326
00:25:56,367 --> 00:25:58,833
Hurry up, come on.

327
00:25:58,833 --> 00:26:01,800
Oh, not bad at all.

328
00:26:01,800 --> 00:26:03,533
We should split up here.

329
00:26:03,533 --> 00:26:06,067
What? We just teamed up, and you're already leaving?

330
00:26:06,067 --> 00:26:07,400
I have to get to work.

331
00:26:07,400 --> 00:26:09,267
Oh, right.

332
00:26:09,267 --> 00:26:13,200
Since I'm free, I'll look around a bit more.

333
00:26:14,400 --> 00:26:16,067
Hello.

334
00:26:16,067 --> 00:26:19,433
Excuse me, by any chance, is there anyone here

335
00:26:19,433 --> 00:26:21,433
who has a scar on their collarbone?

336
00:26:21,433 --> 00:26:24,867
Someone with a dark face and a tall build?

337
00:26:24,867 --> 00:26:26,433
Have you worked with anyone like that before?

338
00:26:26,433 --> 00:26:27,800
No.

339
00:26:27,800 --> 00:26:29,467
Thank you.

340
00:26:32,300 --> 00:26:33,400
Jeong Woo!

341
00:26:33,400 --> 00:26:34,933
Oh, Dong Min.

342
00:26:34,933 --> 00:26:36,233
[Muchang Police Station]
What brings you here so early?

343
00:26:36,233 --> 00:26:37,267
Hello.

344
00:26:37,267 --> 00:26:39,200
Well, actually,

345
00:26:39,200 --> 00:26:41,067
I was walking last night

346
00:26:41,067 --> 00:26:44,267
and saw a suspicious person
lurking at the village entrance.

347
00:26:44,267 --> 00:26:46,167
Oh really? Why didn't you report it?

348
00:26:46,167 --> 00:26:48,067
Please do more night patrols.

349
00:26:48,067 --> 00:26:51,100
Got it, got it. We'll step up patrols.

350
00:26:51,100 --> 00:26:52,267
Keep up the good work.

351
00:26:52,267 --> 00:26:53,967
- Yes.
- Bye.

352
00:26:53,967 --> 00:26:57,733
Let's keep up our night patrols.

353
00:26:59,833 --> 00:27:04,533
Patrols are stronger, list is ready.

354
00:27:05,167 --> 00:27:08,733
Now, I just need to protect Ms. Bu Se Mi.

355
00:27:23,500 --> 00:27:24,533
Miss.

356
00:27:24,533 --> 00:27:26,600
There's a guy named Lee Se Joon here.

357
00:27:26,600 --> 00:27:29,067
He works night shifts every day.

358
00:27:29,067 --> 00:27:31,567
We should check him out.

359
00:27:31,567 --> 00:27:33,133
Okay.

360
00:27:33,133 --> 00:27:36,633
Stay here. I'll go investigate.

361
00:28:07,567 --> 00:28:09,200
Miss!

362
00:28:15,400 --> 00:28:16,433
Where are you?

363
00:28:16,433 --> 00:28:18,533
<i>He just went into Muchang Supermarket Alley.</i>

364
00:28:18,533 --> 00:28:20,000
<i>I think it's him.</i>

365
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:22,200
Got it, I'm on my way.

366
00:29:03,833 --> 00:29:05,867
Darn it.

367
00:29:25,433 --> 00:29:27,133
Get up.

368
00:29:28,767 --> 00:29:30,567
It hurts.

369
00:29:30,567 --> 00:29:32,000
He has no scar.

370
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:33,967
Hey, what's wrong with you guys?

371
00:29:33,967 --> 00:29:35,033
It's you, right?

372
00:29:35,033 --> 00:29:36,533
You were the one who
attacked her yesterday, right?

373
00:29:36,533 --> 00:29:38,433
What are you talking about?

374
00:29:38,433 --> 00:29:41,167
Didn't you break the CCTV?

375
00:29:42,567 --> 00:29:44,567
I heard they were hiring at Mu Si Market,

376
00:29:44,567 --> 00:29:47,300
I just did what I was told and got paid for it.

377
00:29:47,300 --> 00:29:49,967
Man, I knew something was off.

378
00:29:49,967 --> 00:29:51,700
Does that person limp?

379
00:29:51,700 --> 00:29:53,767
We only communicated via phone.

380
00:29:53,767 --> 00:29:56,200
I don't know anything about him.

381
00:29:56,200 --> 00:30:00,033
I just did what they told me, they said
I'd get 50,000 for each CCTV I broke,

382
00:30:00,033 --> 00:30:02,533
so I worked hard for it.

383
00:30:02,533 --> 00:30:05,167
Then how did you know the CCTV routes?

384
00:30:08,733 --> 00:30:10,700
That guy sent me all the details.

385
00:30:10,700 --> 00:30:12,633
Including all the patrol routes.

386
00:30:12,633 --> 00:30:17,040
[Mu Si Market]

387
00:30:53,667 --> 00:30:56,233
Wow, he's fast.

388
00:30:56,233 --> 00:30:57,967
Ah, we lost him.

389
00:30:57,967 --> 00:31:02,667
By the way, earlier, you asked if he was limping, right?

390
00:31:02,667 --> 00:31:05,533
Are you talking about that driver?

391
00:31:05,533 --> 00:31:06,767
Yes.

392
00:31:06,767 --> 00:31:08,800
The only recent newcomers to Muchang

393
00:31:08,800 --> 00:31:11,733
are the driver and seasonal farm workers.

394
00:31:11,733 --> 00:31:13,333
That's right.

395
00:31:14,367 --> 00:31:18,000
Hey, let's call it a day.

396
00:31:18,000 --> 00:31:19,633
Okay.

397
00:31:26,067 --> 00:31:28,500
[Gil Ho Se's Resume]
Why hasn't he checked this?

398
00:31:28,500 --> 00:31:30,333
[Attorney Lee]

399
00:31:32,733 --> 00:31:37,500
<i>The subscriber you dialed is unavailable.
You will be connected to voicemail.</i>

400
00:31:52,367 --> 00:31:54,533
Who the heck are you guys?

401
00:31:54,533 --> 00:31:55,733
Hey.

402
00:31:55,733 --> 00:31:58,367
Where's Ga Seon Woo?

403
00:31:58,367 --> 00:32:00,767
That's what I want to know.

404
00:32:00,767 --> 00:32:03,933
Ah, that lunatic.

405
00:32:03,933 --> 00:32:06,333
Boss, what about our money?

406
00:32:06,333 --> 00:32:09,733
Do you know who I am?

407
00:32:09,733 --> 00:32:15,167
Attorney Lee Don. We're not in the mood for games.

408
00:32:15,167 --> 00:32:18,433
Why? Did Ga Seon Woo rip you off?

409
00:32:18,433 --> 00:32:20,700
You punk.

410
00:32:20,700 --> 00:32:23,667
People are all talking down to me.

411
00:32:23,667 --> 00:32:26,367
I'll give you all the money Ga Seon Woo owes.

412
00:32:26,367 --> 00:32:28,600
I'm loaded.

413
00:32:34,200 --> 00:32:36,933
But why should we trust you?

414
00:32:36,933 --> 00:32:39,467
How did you find me?

415
00:32:39,467 --> 00:32:41,400
That's our specialty.

416
00:32:41,400 --> 00:32:43,000
Really?

417
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:45,500
I'm looking for Ga Seon Woo too.

418
00:32:46,933 --> 00:32:49,133
100 million if you find Ga Seon Woo.

419
00:32:49,133 --> 00:32:52,600
Until then10 million deduction daily. Deal?

420
00:32:54,267 --> 00:32:56,033
Ah, this is frustrating.

421
00:32:56,033 --> 00:32:58,533
Another day's already passing.

422
00:33:01,400 --> 00:33:04,033
Are you joking, punk?

423
00:33:04,033 --> 00:33:06,400
Soon, 10 million won will be deducted.

424
00:33:06,400 --> 00:33:08,933
Pay the deposit of 50 million won.

425
00:33:08,933 --> 00:33:10,933
I got it, so let me go.

426
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:14,380
Hey.

427
00:33:25,300 --> 00:33:27,067
50 million won for the deposit.

428
00:33:30,133 --> 00:33:31,640
Transfer it.

429
00:33:36,467 --> 00:33:37,867
[Ms. Bu Se Mi]

430
00:33:37,867 --> 00:33:39,667
[Gil Ho Se's Resume]

431
00:33:41,567 --> 00:33:43,533
[Shuttle Bus Driver]

432
00:33:43,533 --> 00:33:47,133
[Mid-40s, had an accident and injured his leg]

433
00:33:47,133 --> 00:33:49,400
[Gil Ho Se]

434
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:56,867
Can you find another person?

435
00:33:58,567 --> 00:34:00,333
An additional 100 million won.

436
00:34:00,333 --> 00:34:02,400
Same terms.

437
00:34:02,400 --> 00:34:03,880
Deal.

438
00:34:05,200 --> 00:34:06,630
Transfer it.

439
00:34:19,633 --> 00:34:21,567
Come this way.

440
00:34:31,500 --> 00:34:33,333
I heard you do a great job here, so I came.

441
00:34:33,333 --> 00:34:35,433
I need a passport.

442
00:34:36,800 --> 00:34:38,067
How long does it take?

443
00:34:38,067 --> 00:34:40,400
Passport takes 3 days.

444
00:34:40,400 --> 00:34:43,133
It's not available for the U.S. or Europe,

445
00:34:43,133 --> 00:34:44,600
but no problem for Southeast Asia.

446
00:34:44,600 --> 00:34:47,300
No problem with money,

447
00:34:47,300 --> 00:34:50,300
so the faster, the better.

448
00:34:50,300 --> 00:34:53,400
Rushing leads to mistakes.

449
00:34:58,233 --> 00:34:59,800
I said I got it.

450
00:34:59,800 --> 00:35:01,933
Just meet the deadline.

451
00:35:04,400 --> 00:35:06,800
Come back in 3 days.

452
00:35:14,567 --> 00:35:17,967
Ms. Bu Se Mi, there's an announcement.

453
00:35:17,967 --> 00:35:21,933
This week, a village volleyball competition
will be held at the elementary school playground.

454
00:35:21,933 --> 00:35:23,367
Please attend.

455
00:35:23,367 --> 00:35:24,733
There's an afterparty too.

456
00:35:24,733 --> 00:35:27,400
Let's celebrate together and have dinner.

457
00:35:27,400 --> 00:35:29,000
- Principal.
- Yes?

458
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:31,500
Are there people coming from other villages?

459
00:35:31,500 --> 00:35:33,500
Well,

460
00:35:33,500 --> 00:35:35,267
Dong Min and Jeong Woo from YBS,

461
00:35:35,267 --> 00:35:37,833
and Dongwaru and upper village chief from OBS.

462
00:35:37,833 --> 00:35:40,400
Mainly upper village folks.

463
00:35:40,400 --> 00:35:41,900
Got it.

464
00:35:41,900 --> 00:35:43,600
Yes.

465
00:35:44,567 --> 00:35:46,000
Good morning, Principal.

466
00:35:46,000 --> 00:35:48,233
Good morning.

467
00:35:51,767 --> 00:35:53,433
Ms. Baek Hye Ji.

468
00:35:54,433 --> 00:35:56,667
Let's talk for a minute.

469
00:35:56,667 --> 00:35:59,600
I need to prepare materials before class.

470
00:36:00,730 --> 00:36:04,067
I'll come to Strawberry Class after class.

471
00:36:04,067 --> 00:36:06,567
Have a good class.

472
00:36:08,433 --> 00:36:10,033
Don't worry.

473
00:36:11,367 --> 00:36:12,880
See you then.

474
00:36:15,167 --> 00:36:16,640
Okay.

475
00:36:17,300 --> 00:36:18,700
Gimme a bite.

476
00:36:18,700 --> 00:36:20,467
- No.
- Just one bite.

477
00:36:20,467 --> 00:36:23,267
- No, I'll eat it all.
- One bite.

478
00:36:23,267 --> 00:36:25,100
Just one bite.

479
00:36:26,767 --> 00:36:29,433
Mister, I'm sorry.

480
00:36:29,433 --> 00:36:31,433
No, are you okay?

481
00:36:31,433 --> 00:36:32,633
I'm fine.

482
00:36:32,633 --> 00:36:35,267
I can change clothes, so it's fine.

483
00:36:35,267 --> 00:36:36,667
Oh, no.

484
00:36:36,667 --> 00:36:38,167
Oh, you spilled it.

485
00:36:38,167 --> 00:36:40,767
Running's dangerous, right?

486
00:36:40,767 --> 00:36:42,167
Let's go in.

487
00:36:42,167 --> 00:36:44,600
Go inside and play.

488
00:37:53,700 --> 00:37:56,400
You got me.

489
00:37:56,400 --> 00:37:59,267
Now, you recognize my footsteps?

490
00:38:10,130 --> 00:38:11,733
Ms. Baek Hye Ji.

491
00:38:11,733 --> 00:38:13,933
Why did you follow me last night?

492
00:38:13,933 --> 00:38:15,700
Are you spying on me?

493
00:38:20,400 --> 00:38:22,030
Yes.

494
00:38:22,733 --> 00:38:24,700
I'm spying on you.

495
00:38:30,833 --> 00:38:33,067
I won't ask who told you to do this,

496
00:38:33,067 --> 00:38:36,267
but now stop playing games and leave Muchang.

497
00:38:36,267 --> 00:38:39,833
I don't want to care about you anymore either.

498
00:38:39,833 --> 00:38:41,533
Please.

499
00:39:26,300 --> 00:39:28,600
Oh, it's Hye Ji.

500
00:39:28,600 --> 00:39:29,733
[Baek Hye Ji]

501
00:39:29,733 --> 00:39:32,000
<i>Call me in 30 minutes.</i>

502
00:39:39,467 --> 00:39:41,467
Yes, Miss.

503
00:39:41,467 --> 00:39:43,133
Are you heading home?

504
00:39:43,133 --> 00:39:44,033
Yes.

505
00:39:44,033 --> 00:39:46,667
Then, please give me a ride home.

506
00:39:46,667 --> 00:39:48,667
Sure, get in.

507
00:39:48,667 --> 00:39:50,900
- Thank you.
- Yes.

508
00:39:59,767 --> 00:40:03,433
Alright, let's go.

509
00:40:16,867 --> 00:40:18,867
Miss, what are you looking for?

510
00:40:20,100 --> 00:40:24,600
Well, I've always wondered about
the shuttle bus's front seats.

511
00:40:26,400 --> 00:40:28,767
Nothing special.

512
00:40:28,767 --> 00:40:31,600
Where do you live, Mr. Gil?

513
00:40:31,600 --> 00:40:34,033
Why ask that?

514
00:40:35,230 --> 00:40:40,167
Well, I came down here
and have been staying at the principal's place.

515
00:40:40,167 --> 00:40:42,400
I'm trying to find a place to live.

516
00:40:44,633 --> 00:40:47,733
But I just got a place through someone I know.

517
00:40:47,733 --> 00:40:48,967
Oh?

518
00:40:48,967 --> 00:40:52,633
Do you know someone here? Who?

519
00:40:52,633 --> 00:40:54,667
Well, I've met most people in this town
at the village welcome party,

520
00:40:54,667 --> 00:40:57,067
so I know everyone
in this neighborhood, more or less.

521
00:40:57,067 --> 00:40:59,000
Oh, I see.

522
00:40:59,000 --> 00:41:00,700
Who is it?

523
00:41:03,067 --> 00:41:05,500
You really wanna know?

524
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:13,800
30, 29, 28, 27.

525
00:41:13,800 --> 00:41:18,133
26, 25, 24, 23...

526
00:41:23,600 --> 00:41:25,400
No way...

527
00:41:27,733 --> 00:41:29,433
Is it the village chief?

528
00:41:31,767 --> 00:41:33,600
It's the village chief.

529
00:41:33,600 --> 00:41:35,000
Ah, right.

530
00:41:35,000 --> 00:41:36,133
How did you know?

531
00:41:36,133 --> 00:41:40,367
Everything and everyone here

532
00:41:40,367 --> 00:41:42,633
goes through the village chief.

533
00:41:42,633 --> 00:41:44,267
Right.

534
00:41:53,600 --> 00:41:56,233
By the way, these days,

535
00:41:56,233 --> 00:42:01,633
the trend is for tough guys to leave
one or two buttons undone on their shirts.

536
00:42:03,630 --> 00:42:05,500
Aren't you hot?

537
00:42:08,400 --> 00:42:12,133
I'm a bit sensitive to the cold.

538
00:42:15,500 --> 00:42:17,867
2, 1, time's up.

539
00:42:22,400 --> 00:42:24,033
Hello, Tae Min?

540
00:42:24,033 --> 00:42:26,133
Yes, I'll be down soon.

541
00:42:26,133 --> 00:42:28,200
Okay.

542
00:42:28,200 --> 00:42:30,000
Ah, yes. Huh?

543
00:42:34,400 --> 00:42:36,133
What was that?

544
00:43:06,200 --> 00:43:08,933
[20-19, Eumjeon-ro 28beon-gil, Muchang-myeon,
Muchang County, Gyeongnam]

545
00:43:30,667 --> 00:43:34,567
[Professor, I'll handle it tomorrow.]

546
00:43:40,067 --> 00:43:42,233
<i>She changed her identity?</i>

547
00:43:43,230 --> 00:43:47,267
<i>Then if that woman dies instead of Kim Yeong Ran,</i>

548
00:43:47,267 --> 00:43:49,500
<i>what happens to Kim Yeong Ran?</i>

549
00:43:49,500 --> 00:43:52,833
<i>If a missing adult shows
no signs of life for five years,</i>

550
00:43:52,833 --> 00:43:55,233
<i>they're declared dead.</i>

551
00:43:55,233 --> 00:43:58,967
<i>If Kim Yeong Ran dies now,
it'll complicate things.</i>

552
00:43:58,967 --> 00:44:03,000
<i>Maybe it wouldn't be such a bad thing
for someone else to die.</i>

553
00:44:12,867 --> 00:44:14,933
[Mom]

554
00:44:17,833 --> 00:44:19,100
Hello.

555
00:44:19,100 --> 00:44:23,067
<i>Come pick me up, Yeong Ran.</i>

556
00:44:36,200 --> 00:44:38,533
Miss, something wrong?

557
00:44:38,533 --> 00:44:41,467
Can you take me to Dongwaru?

558
00:44:41,467 --> 00:44:43,267
Sure, get in.

559
00:45:01,100 --> 00:45:02,367
Madam!

560
00:45:02,367 --> 00:45:04,867
Time to go home!

561
00:45:04,867 --> 00:45:07,467
What are you talking about?

562
00:45:08,867 --> 00:45:11,467
My daughter will pick me up.

563
00:45:11,467 --> 00:45:15,000
Madam, how about the bill...

564
00:45:17,200 --> 00:45:19,200
Don't you know my daughter?

565
00:45:19,200 --> 00:45:23,133
My daughter, Kim... Se Mi.

566
00:45:23,133 --> 00:45:25,933
You mean Ms. Bu Se Mi, right?

567
00:45:25,933 --> 00:45:30,233
No one here gets it on the first try.

568
00:45:30,233 --> 00:45:32,733
Hello, you come for her?

569
00:45:33,833 --> 00:45:35,467
Sorry.

570
00:45:36,667 --> 00:45:38,000
She hasn't paid yet.

571
00:45:38,000 --> 00:45:40,900
I'll pay you when I get home.

572
00:45:40,900 --> 00:45:44,267
Mom, let's go.

573
00:45:44,267 --> 00:45:48,267
Mom, why did you drink so much alone?

574
00:45:48,267 --> 00:45:49,660
Let's go.

575
00:45:51,400 --> 00:45:52,667
This town's weird.

576
00:45:52,667 --> 00:45:57,067
No one here gets it on the first try.

577
00:46:24,400 --> 00:46:26,000
It's okay.

578
00:46:30,067 --> 00:46:33,467
[Changhyeon Police Station]

579
00:46:33,467 --> 00:46:35,233
What brings you here?

580
00:46:35,233 --> 00:46:37,460
- Oh, my.
- Found her collapsed on the street.

581
00:46:37,460 --> 00:46:39,467
She looks like she's heavily drunk.

582
00:46:41,100 --> 00:46:44,667
Oh, she drank a lot, couldn't even speak properly.

583
00:46:44,667 --> 00:46:47,367
Do you know her?

584
00:46:47,367 --> 00:46:49,533
Huh?

585
00:46:49,533 --> 00:46:51,667
Kim Yeong Ran.

586
00:46:51,667 --> 00:46:53,667
My daughter.

587
00:46:56,000 --> 00:46:59,433
My daughter, Kim Yeong Ran.

588
00:46:59,433 --> 00:47:02,500
[Teacher ID: Bu Se Mi]
She's a stranger.

589
00:47:02,500 --> 00:47:06,167
She drank too much, I guess.

590
00:47:06,167 --> 00:47:08,833
Must've been tough. Thank you.

591
00:47:08,833 --> 00:47:11,733
We'll ensure her safe return once sober.

592
00:47:11,733 --> 00:47:13,767
Please take care of her.

593
00:47:16,367 --> 00:47:19,800
Hey!

594
00:47:21,867 --> 00:47:24,033
Ma'am.

595
00:47:24,033 --> 00:47:27,600
Get your act together and straighten up your life.

596
00:47:27,600 --> 00:47:30,067
Don't make your kids suffer.

597
00:47:32,867 --> 00:47:36,367
Kim Yeong Ran!

598
00:47:38,567 --> 00:47:40,267
Wait, Miss.

599
00:47:42,233 --> 00:47:45,300
Is it okay to leave her like this?

600
00:47:45,300 --> 00:47:47,200
Why?

601
00:47:47,200 --> 00:47:48,700
I'm a bit worried.

602
00:47:48,700 --> 00:47:49,700
About what?

603
00:47:49,700 --> 00:47:52,167
What exactly are you worried about?

604
00:47:52,167 --> 00:47:53,867
Huh?

605
00:47:53,867 --> 00:47:56,533
Do you think I went too far?

606
00:47:56,533 --> 00:47:58,933
The theft charge they're blasting on the news.

607
00:47:58,933 --> 00:48:00,667
I didn't steal the sanitary pads.

608
00:48:00,667 --> 00:48:03,000
I considered stealing,
but changed my mind and put them back.

609
00:48:03,000 --> 00:48:04,800
But I got caught at the worst possible moment.

610
00:48:04,800 --> 00:48:07,833
That convenience store owner
pinned every theft on me.

611
00:48:07,833 --> 00:48:09,967
Then he demanded settlement money.

612
00:48:11,500 --> 00:48:14,800
Do you know what Mom said when she showed up?

613
00:48:14,800 --> 00:48:18,267
'Yeong Ran, just go to juvie for a while.'

614
00:48:18,267 --> 00:48:20,400
'I can't afford to pay.'

615
00:48:20,400 --> 00:48:23,467
That's just cruel, you know?

616
00:48:24,567 --> 00:48:26,867
Kim Yeong Ran!

617
00:48:28,500 --> 00:48:31,333
Ah, you wicked...

618
00:48:58,650 --> 00:49:00,550
Let's go home now.

619
00:49:53,633 --> 00:49:55,933
Hello.

620
00:49:55,933 --> 00:49:57,700
Hello.

621
00:49:59,867 --> 00:50:01,500
Oh, my.

622
00:50:05,600 --> 00:50:07,167
Honey.

623
00:50:07,167 --> 00:50:08,233
Honey.

624
00:50:08,233 --> 00:50:10,333
Hello.

625
00:50:10,333 --> 00:50:12,133
Oh, no, we're late.

626
00:50:17,700 --> 00:50:18,933
Hey, lift it up. Quickly.

627
00:50:18,933 --> 00:50:20,800
One, two, three.

628
00:50:23,133 --> 00:50:25,633
Hey, Tae Min.

629
00:50:25,633 --> 00:50:27,224
Okay.

630
00:50:30,333 --> 00:50:32,000
Honey.

631
00:50:35,300 --> 00:50:36,833
Principal.

632
00:50:36,833 --> 00:50:38,233
Principal.

633
00:50:38,233 --> 00:50:39,267
- This...
- Oh, Mr. Gil.

634
00:50:39,267 --> 00:50:42,433
- You can leave it here.
- Hello.

635
00:50:42,433 --> 00:50:44,767
It's really trendy these days.

636
00:50:44,767 --> 00:50:46,390
Oh, hello.

637
00:50:50,967 --> 00:50:54,133
Jenny, take some chairs over there.

638
00:50:54,133 --> 00:50:56,867
More this way.

639
00:51:00,288 --> 00:51:02,168
Okay.

640
00:51:03,900 --> 00:51:06,433
Ms. Choi, take a photo for me.

641
00:51:10,300 --> 00:51:11,400
Ready?

642
00:51:11,400 --> 00:51:13,700
One, two, three.

643
00:51:13,700 --> 00:51:16,100
One, two, three.

644
00:51:17,533 --> 00:51:20,400
Anyway, our chairman's taste was so refined.

645
00:51:20,400 --> 00:51:25,767
Hey, how much could
we get selling these secondhand?

646
00:51:25,767 --> 00:51:28,600
Probably around 30 million won?

647
00:51:28,600 --> 00:51:30,300
That much?

648
00:51:30,300 --> 00:51:33,367
Hey, selling just a few of these
could beat our annual salary.

649
00:51:33,367 --> 00:51:34,767
Exactly.

650
00:51:34,767 --> 00:51:37,667
We can't find the will,
and there's no money coming in.

651
00:51:37,667 --> 00:51:40,867
Anyway, I have to give you credit
for your cleverness.

652
00:51:40,867 --> 00:51:41,900
What did you say?

653
00:51:41,900 --> 00:51:43,733
It's a compliment. A compliment!

654
00:51:43,733 --> 00:51:45,467
Hey, you take that photo.

655
00:51:45,467 --> 00:51:48,500
Ah, I said it's a compliment. Really!

656
00:51:48,500 --> 00:51:53,300
Being the lady of this house,
I'd like some liquor...

657
00:51:56,333 --> 00:51:59,000
What's liquor? Sounds so old-fashioned.

658
00:51:59,000 --> 00:52:00,767
Whiskey.

659
00:52:00,767 --> 00:52:03,667
Whether it's whiskey or liquor, it's all the same.

660
00:52:03,667 --> 00:52:05,600
Butler, you went to Gukmin School, right?

661
00:52:05,600 --> 00:52:06,400
Yeah.

662
00:52:06,400 --> 00:52:07,833
I went to elementary school.

663
00:52:07,833 --> 00:52:09,500
The generation gap...

664
00:52:09,500 --> 00:52:11,933
Yeah, you're so amazing.

665
00:52:14,233 --> 00:52:16,633
Alright then.

666
00:52:16,633 --> 00:52:19,280
Should I post a photo after so long?

667
00:52:21,367 --> 00:52:27,267
[Resume]
Restaurant assistant, housekeeper, childcare aide.

668
00:52:27,267 --> 00:52:29,733
Laundry duty.

669
00:52:39,567 --> 00:52:42,733
Madam, where should I put this?

670
00:52:45,533 --> 00:52:47,633
Madam...

671
00:52:48,833 --> 00:52:50,500
Yeah...

672
00:52:52,433 --> 00:52:54,400
Let me see.

673
00:52:54,400 --> 00:52:59,267
Put the Hanwoo beef
in the fridge's third compartment.

674
00:52:59,267 --> 00:53:03,400
And place the pears in the fridge's bottom drawer.

675
00:53:03,400 --> 00:53:07,267
Leave the wild pine mushrooms here on the table.

676
00:53:07,267 --> 00:53:10,400
We'll have them for dinner later.

677
00:53:14,400 --> 00:53:17,767
Nice.

678
00:53:18,633 --> 00:53:20,367
That's right.

679
00:53:22,033 --> 00:53:23,633
Nice.

680
00:53:32,367 --> 00:53:35,132
It's okay! It's okay!

681
00:53:35,132 --> 00:53:37,033
Good job.

682
00:53:37,033 --> 00:53:39,267
Good job.

683
00:53:46,933 --> 00:53:49,367
Good job.

684
00:54:03,533 --> 00:54:04,967
Enjoy your meal.

685
00:54:04,967 --> 00:54:06,900
Thank you.

686
00:54:07,500 --> 00:54:08,967
Enjoy your meal.

687
00:54:08,967 --> 00:54:11,433
Ms. Bu, hurry up and sit down to eat.

688
00:54:11,433 --> 00:54:13,400
I'll eat later.

689
00:54:13,400 --> 00:54:15,700
Enjoy your meal.

690
00:54:15,700 --> 00:54:18,233
[Gil Ho Se, Inmate ID Card]

691
00:54:18,233 --> 00:54:21,150
[Gil Ho Se's Resume]

692
00:54:21,150 --> 00:54:24,667
[Mid-40s, shuttle-bus driver,
left leg injured in an accident]

693
00:54:34,033 --> 00:54:37,333
Apple Class and Strawberry Class, enjoy your meal.

694
00:54:37,333 --> 00:54:39,433
- Yes.
- Yes.

695
00:54:40,367 --> 00:54:42,133
It's delicious.

696
00:54:42,133 --> 00:54:43,767
[Attorney Lee]
The meat is so delicious.

697
00:54:43,767 --> 00:54:45,033
Just let me know if you need more.

698
00:54:45,033 --> 00:54:46,733
Okay.

699
00:54:48,700 --> 00:54:50,633
It's delicious.

700
00:54:59,200 --> 00:55:01,100
Enjoy your meal.

701
00:55:01,600 --> 00:55:03,000
Yes, it's me.

702
00:55:03,000 --> 00:55:07,200
Madam. Madam, I think that punk Gil Ho Se is the one.

703
00:55:09,600 --> 00:55:11,600
Understood.

704
00:55:19,633 --> 00:55:22,967
[Driver Gil Ho Se]

705
00:55:29,984 --> 00:55:33,967
[Ms. Bu Se Mi]
<i>Sir, could you come to our house by nine?</i>

706
00:55:33,967 --> 00:55:36,000
<i>I have a favor to ask.</i>

707
00:55:37,728 --> 00:55:39,676
This is good.

708
00:55:39,676 --> 00:55:42,040
Enjoy your meal.

709
00:55:47,200 --> 00:55:49,067
Ho Se!

710
00:55:49,067 --> 00:55:51,600
Come here and have a drink with me!

711
00:55:51,600 --> 00:55:54,467
I'll just go to the bathroom quickly.

712
00:55:54,467 --> 00:55:56,267
- Make it quick.
- Okay.

713
00:55:56,267 --> 00:55:59,667
- We're out of alcohol.
- Oh, right.

714
00:56:09,733 --> 00:56:11,567
I...

715
00:56:13,900 --> 00:56:15,267
No.

716
00:56:15,267 --> 00:56:16,500
I don't think that way.

717
00:56:16,500 --> 00:56:17,500
Wait, look.

718
00:56:17,500 --> 00:56:20,233
Our pretty Jeong Hwa, how could he...

719
00:56:20,233 --> 00:56:22,433
- Honestly, I...
- Principal.

720
00:56:22,433 --> 00:56:25,333
- Yes?
- Where's Ms. Bu Se Mi?

721
00:56:25,333 --> 00:56:26,867
- I...
- Huh?

722
00:56:26,867 --> 00:56:31,300
Wait, she was here just a moment ago.

723
00:56:31,300 --> 00:56:33,567
Where did she go?

724
00:56:33,567 --> 00:56:35,300
- Why? What's wrong?
- Actually.

725
00:56:35,300 --> 00:56:37,733
Honestly, I like Jeong Woo.

726
00:56:37,733 --> 00:56:39,733
- I...
- I like Jeong Woo.

727
00:56:39,733 --> 00:56:41,867
Jeong Woo's nice.

728
00:56:46,433 --> 00:56:49,100
He's such a kind person.

729
00:56:55,933 --> 00:56:57,933
Jeong Woo... Jeong Woo?

730
00:56:57,933 --> 00:57:01,067
Jeong Woo, don't you remember that?

731
00:57:06,112 --> 00:57:08,313
Oh, it's fun.

732
00:57:09,067 --> 00:57:11,100
- Mi Seon.
- Oh, Tae Min.

733
00:57:11,100 --> 00:57:12,667
Where's Hye Ji?

734
00:57:12,667 --> 00:57:14,967
She wanted vanilla ice cream earlier.

735
00:57:14,967 --> 00:57:16,700
Huh? Hye Ji's right here.

736
00:57:16,700 --> 00:57:19,233
- Look.
- Wait a minute.

737
00:57:19,233 --> 00:57:20,700
No, she's right here, Tae Min.

738
00:57:20,700 --> 00:57:22,033
Hye Ji's right here.

739
00:57:22,033 --> 00:57:24,267
Just give it to her here.

740
00:57:25,333 --> 00:57:27,033
- That's Hye Ji's.
- Okay, Hye Ji.

741
00:57:27,033 --> 00:57:28,767
Hye Ji who loves vanilla.

742
00:57:28,767 --> 00:57:30,867
Give me some too.

743
00:57:38,233 --> 00:57:43,000
<i>By the way, earlier, you asked if he was limping, right?</i>

744
00:57:43,000 --> 00:57:45,900
<i>Are you talking about that driver?</i>

745
00:57:45,900 --> 00:57:49,200
<i>Yes, only recent newcomers to Muchang</i>

746
00:57:49,200 --> 00:57:52,300
<i>are the driver and seasonal farm workers.</i>

747
00:57:52,300 --> 00:57:55,167
Since Jeong Woo's acting this way...

748
00:57:56,267 --> 00:57:57,933
- Mi Seon, Mi Seon.
- Huh?

749
00:57:57,933 --> 00:57:59,133
Where'd Mr. Gil go?

750
00:57:59,133 --> 00:58:01,000
Mr. Gil?

751
00:58:01,000 --> 00:58:02,400
He must be somewhere.

752
00:58:02,400 --> 00:58:04,200
Oh, Ho Se?

753
00:58:04,200 --> 00:58:07,833
He went to the bathroom to pee earlier.

754
00:58:07,833 --> 00:58:09,767
Where did he go?

755
00:58:09,767 --> 00:58:16,300
If he went to pee, he's in the bathroom.
Why keep looking elsewhere?

756
00:58:16,300 --> 00:58:19,200
Dong Min, what's wrong?

757
00:58:19,200 --> 00:58:20,867
Dong Min.

758
00:58:20,867 --> 00:58:22,567
Dong Min!

759
00:59:06,000 --> 00:59:08,833
Ms. Bu Se Mi.

760
00:59:47,167 --> 00:59:49,433
Who exactly are you?

761
00:59:50,267 --> 00:59:54,067
Miss, calm down.

762
01:00:35,467 --> 01:00:40,267
[Jeon Dong Min]

763
01:01:42,000 --> 01:01:44,500
Friend! Are you okay?

764
01:01:44,500 --> 01:01:46,233
Snap out of it, friend!

765
01:01:46,233 --> 01:01:47,600
Can you see me?

766
01:01:47,600 --> 01:01:49,500
Yeong Ran, are you hurt?

767
01:01:49,500 --> 01:01:51,433
Hye Ji.

768
01:02:00,167 --> 01:02:01,200
Baek Hye Ji.

769
01:02:01,200 --> 01:02:02,900
No.

770
01:02:45,933 --> 01:02:50,067
Goodbye. Ms. Bu Se Mi.

771
01:03:11,333 --> 01:03:17,067
<i>♫ Starting to be born again ♫</i>

772
01:03:29,667 --> 01:03:32,667
<i>♫ Now is the time ♫</i>

773
01:03:32,667 --> 01:03:40,767
<i>♫ Even hidden scars will shine ♫</i>

774
01:03:40,767 --> 01:03:43,833
<i>♫ I share the light ♫</i>

775
01:03:43,833 --> 01:03:50,300
<i>♫ I'll brighten the days shrouded in darkness ♫</i>

776
01:03:50,300 --> 01:03:51,933
This was Gil Ho Se's room.

777
01:03:51,933 --> 01:03:53,767
There must be something here.

778
01:03:53,767 --> 01:03:55,700
Lee Mi Seon, principal of Iseon Kindergarten.

779
01:03:55,700 --> 01:03:57,033
Let's not involve family.

780
01:03:57,033 --> 01:03:58,633
Let me make a proposal.

781
01:03:58,633 --> 01:04:00,133
Doctor!

782
01:04:00,133 --> 01:04:02,467
In exchange for that proposal,
how much will you give me?

783
01:04:02,467 --> 01:04:04,100
As much as you want.

784
01:04:04,100 --> 01:04:06,067
You miss Ms. Bu Se Mi a lot, right?

785
01:04:06,067 --> 01:04:07,800
I have something to say.

786
01:04:07,800 --> 01:04:08,867
I've missed you.

787
01:04:08,867 --> 01:04:10,533
Huh? What?

788
01:04:10,533 --> 01:04:12,633
Even if everything fails,

789
01:04:12,633 --> 01:04:14,933
I'll kill Ga Seon Yeong myself then.

790
01:04:14,933 --> 01:04:18,333
[Gaseong Group Emergency Press Conference]
You'll never be able to go back to your old life.

